er.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{34}{7}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e8d21f26-67b9-5b1e-b9e7-725f74bfd9d4" :answer/id #uuid "e8d21f26-67b9-5b1e-b9e7-725f74bfd9d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{76}{7}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e5a37119-64a0-594b-a7bb-6f870c3ecc3e" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a37119-64a0-594b-a7bb-6f870c3ecc3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["7534c7ed-b9b9-5a4e-b7cc-648e83cbe230" "7b4eb6cc-0bc2-52a2-b07f-504b6d6ecb53" "5f260668-83d5-5737-be7a-fcd41740577c" "c55cc9ed-9a42-5e6f-9fff-988edf9b714f" "e8d21f26-67b9-5b1e-b9e7-725f74bfd9d4"] :answer-field/correct "7b4eb6cc-0bc2-52a2-b07f-504b6d6ecb53" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "24687af9-7fd4-5bfe-b0b9-67927f085480" :question/id #uuid "24687af9-7fd4-5bfe-b0b9-67927f085480" :question/problem "If $\\cos x=\\frac{5}{7},$ then $-4\\cos (x+10\\pi )+2=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x=\\cos (x+2\\cdot 5\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x+10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=\\frac{5}{7},$ then $\\cos (x+10\\pi )=\\frac{5}{7}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\cos (x+10\\pi )+2 & =-4(\\frac{5}{7})+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{7}+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["e5a37119-64a0-594b-a7bb-6f870c3ecc3e"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "60d115bc-5abe-5b32-a617-3d115b680270" :answer/id #uuid "60d115bc-5abe-5b32-a617-3d115b680270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{46}{11}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d1481b75-880b-5cb5-95b2-1b161d8953b2" :answer/id #uuid "d1481b75-880b-5cb5-95b2-1b161d8953b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{34}{11}" :db/ensure